{
  "_": [
    "The 241 Doré plates, each anchored to the verse it depicts.",
    "",
    "THIS FILE IS THE DECISION, not a cache of one. It was produced on",
    "2026-08-28 by a reconciliation that read the caption printed under each",
    "plate with OCR and voted it against the Wikipedia table and",
    "catholic-resources.org's own index -- 88 anchors the witnesses agreed",
    "on, 132 they disputed, 21 only one of them placed. That code has been",
    "deleted: a vote whose result is written down has nothing left to decide,",
    "and OCR is not a pure function of a file, so re-running it on every",
    "rebuild would have been a re-decision wearing a rebuild's clothes.",
    "",
    "IT IS FIVE FIELDS BECAUSE FIVE ARE READ. Every witness's reading was",
    "kept here at first -- what the caption said, what Wikipedia said, which",
    "one carried the book and which the verse. With the code that weighed",
    "them gone, none of it was read by anything: not by this pipeline, not by",
    "the sync, not by the site. It is one `git show ca1b76d` away and that is",
    "where evidence for a decision already taken belongs, rather than in",
    "7,000 lines of a file whose operative content is 1,200.",
    "",
    "WHY IT IS TRACKED HERE AND NOT IN THE CORPUS'S raw/. raw/ is the record",
    "of what a source SAID, write-once and carried by git-lfs; this is what",
    "we CONCLUDED about what it said, and 132 of the 241 are a judgment",
    "between witnesses that disagreed. It belongs with pipeline/corrections/",
    "and pipeline/overrides/ -- editorial decisions, in the public",
    "repository, applied to corpus data by a scraper that reads both.",
    "",
    "TO CHANGE AN ANCHOR, edit `verse` here and say why in the commit. There",
    "is no pipeline to re-run: `dore.py` writes plates.json straight from",
    "this file. A null verse anchors the plate to its chapter instead, which",
    "the site places before the first verse it has; nothing uses that today.",
    "",
    "The masters are at MASTER_URL in dore.py, one per plate_id, and they are",
    "in the corpus under raw/dore/plates/. `title` is the plate's name as",
    "catholic-resources.org gives it, and it is what the site's caption",
    "prints."
  ],
  "decided_at": "2026-08-28",
  "ocr_engine": "tesseract 5.5.3",
